-- title:
--   Regularity at all affine places equals integrality over k[̃ j,̃ j_N]
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive natural number and $k$ a field in which $N$ is invertible in the weak sense that the image of $N$ in $k$ is nonzero. Work inside the field $L = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by the two series $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{reduction mod }k\text{ of the integral power series }\mathrm{jNum})$ and $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N$, the substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$ applied to the former; write $\tilde j = \mathrm{jGeomGen}\,k\,N$ and $\tilde j_N = \mathrm{jNGeomGen}\,k\,N$ for these two series regarded as elements of $L$. Let $f \in L$. Here a place of $L$ over $k$ is a valuation subring $\mathcal O \subseteq L$ which contains the image of $k$, is not all of $L$, and is a principal ideal ring; such a place is called affine, `IsAffineGeomPlace k N`, precisely when both $\tilde j$ and $\tilde j_N$ lie in $\mathcal O$. The theorem asserts the equivalence: $f$ belongs to the valuation subring of every affine place of $L$ over $k$ if and only if $f$ is integral over the $k$-subalgebra $k[\tilde j, \tilde j_N]$ of $L$ generated by the two series.
--
--   This identifies the ring of functions in the modular function field that are regular at every place where $\tilde j$ and $\tilde j_N$ are regular with the integral closure of $k[\tilde j,\tilde j_N]$, i.e. with the coordinate ring of the normalisation of the affine modular curve in the geometric (Laurent-series) model used throughout the level-$N$ theory. It is used in the construction of mod $p$ and $q$-expansion dictionaries for modular forms and in the algebra-homomorphism statements at full level.
